      <Docs>
        <param name="associatedUris">The list of URIs to be parsed. The order of the URIs in the list
                                  matters. The method iterates through the list and stops at the first
                                  URI that can be parsed into a valid phone number. It is recommended to
                                  place the URIs that are most likely to contain a valid phone number at
                                  the beginning of the list.</param>
        <param name="countryIso">The country ISO code to be used for parsing.</param>
        <summary>Parses the associated URIs into a <c>ParsedPhoneNumber</c> object.</summary>
        <returns>A <c>ParsedPhoneNumber</c> object representing the first successfully parsed
            phone number from the provided list or an error if no numbers could be parsed.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>Parses the associated URIs into a <c>ParsedPhoneNumber</c> object.</para>
          <para>This method attempts to parse the provided list of URIs into a valid phone number.
            The order of the URIs in the list is significant; it is recommended to prioritize URIs
            that are more likely to contain a valid phone number by placing them at the beginning of
            the list. The method will iterate through the list and return the first URI that can be
            successfully parsed into a valid phone number.</para>
          <para>
            <format type="text/html">
              <a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/PhoneNumberManager#parsePhoneNumber(java.util.List%3Candroid.net.Uri%3E,%20java.lang.String)" title="Reference documentation">Java documentation for <code>android.telephony.PhoneNumberManager.parsePhoneNumber(java.util.List&lt;android.net.Uri&gt;, java.lang.String)</code>.</a>
            </format>
          </para>
